# 11. File Description

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `coremodel.slx` | Main healthy isolator Simulink model |
| `coremodel.slxc` | Automatically generated Simulink cache for `coremodel.slx` |
| `coremodelfault.slx` | Isolator model containing the mechanical/fault simulation branch |
| `coremodelfault.slxc` | Automatically generated Simulink cache for the fault model |
| `featurecheck.m` | Checks/validates extracted features and their values |
| `featuresextraction.m` | Extracts statistical and operation-level features from simulation measurements |
| `healthy_dataset.mat` | Processed dataset containing healthy-condition samples/features |
| `healthy_feature_check.mat` | Saved results used for checking healthy feature consistency |
| `healthy_original.mat` | Saved original/raw healthy simulation data |
| `healthy_run_01.mat` | Data from an individual healthy simulation run |
| `healthydata.m` | Script used for generating/processing healthy-condition simulation data |
| `init.m` | Initializes model parameters and MATLAB workspace variables |
| `isolator_config_demo.m` | Demonstrates/configures isolator project parameters |
| `isolator_project_config.mat` | Saved configuration parameters for the isolator project |
| `mcxn547_adc_model.m` | MATLAB representation of ADC/data-acquisition behaviour associated with the NXP MCXN547 processing stage |
| `model.slx` | Earlier/development Simulink model; retain only if still required |
| `operation_features.m` | Calculates the operation-level feature vector from V, I, torque and position |
| `selftest_blocks.m` | Performs checks/self-tests associated with signal-processing or model blocks |
| `shaft_friction_comparison.mat` | Saved healthy/faulty shaft-friction comparison data |
| `untitled1.slx` | Development/test Simulink model; rename or remove if no longer required |
| `README.md` | Project documentation and execution instructions |

---

# 12. `.slxc` Files

Files such as:

```text
coremodel.slxc
coremodelfault.slxc
```

are Simulink cache files.

They are generated automatically to improve compilation/simulation speed.

They are **not the actual Simulink models**.

The important source files are:

```text
coremodel.slx
coremodelfault.slx
```

The `.slxc` files may normally be excluded from Git/GitHub because MATLAB can regenerate them.

A `.gitignore` entry can therefore contain:

```gitignore
*.slxc
slprj/
*.asv
```

---

# 13. Recommended Project Workflow

```text
Create physical isolator model
            ↓
Configure DC motor and mechanical system
            ↓
Add Voltage / Current / Torque / Position sensors
            ↓
Create isolator controller
            ↓
Run healthy simulation
            ↓
Verify V, I, Torque and Position
            ↓
Generate repeated healthy runs
            ↓
Extract operation features
            ↓
Generate healthy dataset
            ↓
Introduce mechanical friction fault
            ↓
Run faulty model
            ↓
Measure V, I, Torque, Angle, Speed and Fault Torque
            ↓
Compare healthy and faulty behaviour
            ↓
Generate labelled fault dataset
            ↓
Normalize/select features
            ↓
Train ANN / ML classifier
            ↓
Validate classifier
            ↓
Prepare model for embedded implementation
            ↓
Target NXP MCXN547 MCU
```

---

# 14. Signal Logging Troubleshooting

If MATLAB reports:

```text
Warning: Did not find any Dataset element using 'Vm'
```

first inspect the dataset:

```matlab
logs = outHealthy.logsout;

disp(string(logs.getElementNames))
```

Do not access logged signals using:

```matlab
logs.Vm
```

Use:

```matlab
logs.get("Vm")
```

provided that `Vm` appears in the dataset.

If it does not appear, enable **Signal Logging** for the corresponding Simulink signal and give the signal the required name.

---

# 15. Important Data-Processing Rule

The electrical and mechanical signals may contain different numbers of samples.

For example:

```text
Vm         : 125231 samples
Im         : 125231 samples
tauNm      : 125231 samples
theta_deg  : 12001 samples
```

This is valid because different parts of the Simscape/Simulink system can have different sampling points.

Therefore use:

```matlab
Vm_sig.Values.Time
Im_sig.Values.Time
tau_sig.Values.Time
theta_sig.Values.Time
```

individually.

Do not simply truncate every signal to the shortest vector.

If signals must be compared sample-by-sample, interpolate them onto a common time vector first.

---

# 16. Current Stage of the Project

The project presently contains the main stages required before ANN training:

```text
Healthy physical model       ✓
Signal measurement           ✓
Controller                    ✓
Healthy simulation           ✓
Healthy dataset              ✓
Feature extraction           ✓
Mechanical fault model       ✓
Friction-fault simulation    ✓
Healthy/fault comparison     ✓

Fault dataset expansion      → Next
Dataset labelling            → Next
ANN training                 → Next
ANN validation               → Next
MCU deployment               → Later
```

The next major step is to generate multiple fault-severity samples instead of relying on a single faulty simulation. The resulting healthy and fault samples can then be combined into a labelled training dataset.
